What:		/sys/kernel/tracing/events/power/gpu_work_period
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Android per-UID GPU work accounting tracepoint consumed by
		GpuService's gpuWork eBPF program.

		The raw event fields, after the common trace header, are:

		  u32 gpu_id
		  u32 uid
		  u64 start_time_ns
		  u64 end_time_ns
		  u64 total_active_duration_ns

		The start and end timestamps use CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW. Each emitted
		period is nonzero, no longer than one second, and does not overlap
		the preceding period for the same UID. Protected GPU work is not
		included.

		KGSL accumulates A6xx CP_ALWAYS_ON_CONTEXT ticks by Android UID,
		converts the 19.2 MHz counter to nanoseconds, clamps active time to
		the reporting interval, and emits active periods every 900 ms.
